      "text": "# Safe Offline Archive Importer\n\n## Design Overview\n\nThis implementation provides a secure, robust ZIP archive importer that addresses common security vulnerabilities and reliability concerns when extracting archives from untrusted sources. The key design principles are:\n\n1. **Path Normalization & Traversal Prevention**: Reject any entry whose normalized path escapes the target directory.\n2. **Symlink/Hardlink Safety**: Never create symlinks or hardlinks during extraction; treat them as regular files or reject them.\n3. **Size Limits**: Enforce maximum uncompressed size, compressed size, and total archive size to prevent zip bombs.\n4. **Streaming Extraction**: Process entries one at a time without loading entire archives into memory.\n5. **Atomic Publication**: Extract to a temporary directory, then atomically rename to the final destination.\n6. **Interrupted Extraction Handling**: Use journaling/checkpointing so partial extractions can be detected and cleaned up.\n7. **Zip Bomb Detection**: Track cumulative uncompressed size and abort if limits are exceeded.\n\n## Security Threats Addressed\n\n| Threat | Mitigation |\n|--------|-----------|\n| Path traversal (`../../etc/passwd`) | Normalize paths, reject absolute paths and `..` components |\n| Zip bomb (huge uncompressed size) | Enforce per-entry and total uncompressed size limits |\n| Symlink attacks | Never create symlinks; reject entries with symlink attributes |\n| Hardlink attacks | Never create hardlinks |\n| Partial extraction corruption | Atomic rename after full extraction; cleanup on failure |\n| Resource exhaustion | Streaming I/O, bounded buffers, size limits |\n| TOCTOU races | Extract to temp dir, verify, then atomic rename |\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSafe offline archive importer for ZIP files.\n\nThis module provides a secure ZIP extraction utility that protects against\npath traversal, zip bombs, symlink attacks, and partial extraction corruption.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport binascii\nimport io\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport stat\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath\nfrom typing import Optional, BinaryIO, Iterator, Tuple, Set\n\n# Try to import compression modules\ntry:\n    import zlib\n    crc32 = zlib.crc32\nexcept ImportError:\n    zlib = None\n    crc32 = binascii.crc32\n\ntry:\n    import bz2\nexcept ImportError:\n    bz2 = None\n\ntry:\n    import lzma\nexcept ImportError:\n    lzma = None\n\ntry:\n    from compression import zstd\nexcept ImportError:\n    zstd = None\n\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"SafeZipImporter\",\n    \"ImportError\",\n    \"PathTraversalError\",\n    \"ZipBombError\",\n    \"SymlinkError\",\n    \"SizeLimitError\",\n    \"ArchiveCorruptionError\",\n    \"ImportResult\",\n]\n\n\nclass ImportError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for archive import errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass PathTraversalError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive entry attempts to escape the target directory.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ZipBombError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive exceeds configured size limits (potential zip bomb).\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SymlinkError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive contains symlink or hardlink entries.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SizeLimitError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a single entry exceeds the maximum allowed size.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ArchiveCorruptionError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the archive is corrupted or unreadable.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ImportResult:\n    \"\"\"Result of an archive import operation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.extracted_files: list[str] = []\n        self.skipped_files: list[str] = []\n        self.total_uncompressed_size: int = 0\n        self.total_compressed_size: int = 0\n        self.entry_count: int = 0\n        self.warnings: list[str] = []\n\n    def __repr__(self):\n        return (\n            f\"ImportResult(extracted={len(self.extracted_files)}, \"\n            f\"skipped={len(self.skipped_files)}, \"\n            f\"total_size={self.total_uncompressed_size}, \"\n            f\"entries={self.entry_count})\"\n        )\n\n\n# ZIP format constants (from the reference implementation)\nZIP_STORED = 0\nZIP_DEFLATED = 8\nZIP_BZIP2 = 12\nZIP_LZMA = 14\nZIP_ZSTANDARD = 93\n\n# End of central directory\nstructEndArchive = b\"<4s4H2LH\"\nstringEndArchive = b\"PK\\005\\006\"",
